{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.RowStandardTableau","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RowStandardTableau","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.Specht","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasisCore"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RowStandardTableau.IsStandard.isRowStandard","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RowStandardTableau.IsStandard.isRowStandard","kind":"theorem","line":243,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RowStandardTableau.lean#L243-L244","doc":"Standard implies row-standard — the inclusion of index sets Lemma 3.14 moves along. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RowStandardTableau.isStandard_sytToTableau","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RowStandardTableau.isStandard_sytToTableau","kind":"theorem","line":237,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RowStandardTableau.lean#L237-L241","doc":"**A standard tableau, read as a filling, is standard** — both halves together. This is the\nmap `Std(μ) → {t : Tableau μ // IsStandard t}` that Lemma 3.14's target side quantifies over. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RowStandardTableau.isColStandard_sytToTableau","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RowStandardTableau.isColStandard_sytToTableau","kind":"theorem","line":216,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RowStandardTableau.lean#L216-L234","doc":"A standard tableau, read as a filling, is column-standard. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RowStandardTableau.entry_lt_entry_of_lt_row","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RowStandardTableau.entry_lt_entry_of_lt_row","kind":"theorem","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RowStandardTableau.lean#L200-L213","doc":"**Column entries increase down a whole column, not just between neighbours** — the column\ntwin of `entry_lt_entry_of_lt`, and, like it, belonging upstream in\n`QOU.BraidKnot.StandardYoungTableau`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RowStandardTableau.instDecidableIsStandard","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RowStandardTableau.instDecidableIsStandard","kind":"instance","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RowStandardTableau.lean#L196-L197","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RowStandardTableau.instDecidableIsColStandard","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RowStandardTableau.instDecidableIsColStandard","kind":"instance","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RowStandardTableau.lean#L193-L194","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RowStandardTableau.IsStandard","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RowStandardTableau.IsStandard","kind":"def","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RowStandardTableau.lean#L190-L191","doc":"**Standard**: row-standard and column-standard. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RowStandardTableau.IsColStandard","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RowStandardTableau.IsColStandard","kind":"def","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RowStandardTableau.lean#L185-L188","doc":"**Column-standard**: within any one column, label order agrees with row order. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RowStandardTableau.isRowStandard_sytToTableau","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RowStandardTableau.isRowStandard_sytToTableau","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RowStandardTableau.lean#L145-L171","doc":"**A standard tableau, read as a filling, is row-standard** — the forgetful map\n`Std(μ) → RowStd(μ)` that Lemma 3.14's target side needs.\n\n`sytToTableau T` is the inverse of `cellLabel T`, so a label `l` sits at the cell `c` with\n`cellLabel T c = l`, and `cellLabel` is literally `T.entry` on that cell. Two labels in the same\nrow with the earlier column therefore compare exactly as their entries do, which is\n`entry_lt_entry_of_lt`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RowStandardTableau.entry_lt_entry_of_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RowStandardTableau.entry_lt_entry_of_lt","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RowStandardTableau.lean#L127-L142","doc":"**Row entries increase across a whole row, not just between neighbours.**\n\nThe transitive closure of `row_strict`, by induction on the right-hand column. The up-left\nclosure of a `YoungDiagram` supplies the intermediate cells: if `(i, j')` is in the diagram then\nso is every `(i, k)` with `k ≤ j'`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RowStandardTableau.card_eq_factorial_of_no_second_column","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RowStandardTableau.card_eq_factorial_of_no_second_column","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RowStandardTableau.lean#L94-L108","doc":"**`n!` row-standard tableaux on a one-column shape** — against exactly one standard tableau.\n\nThis is the quantitative form of the gap the module docstring names: it is why Mathas' Lemma\n3.14 cannot be stated against the standard-pair index set `HeckeMurphyYoung.MurphyIndex`, and\nwhy `span_murphySum_one_conjugates_eq_top` had to be phrased over conjugating permutations\ninstead of over tableaux. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RowStandardTableau.equivTableauOfNoSecondColumn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RowStandardTableau.equivTableauOfNoSecondColumn","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RowStandardTableau.lean#L86-L92","doc":"On a one-column shape the row-standard tableaux are **all** the fillings. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RowStandardTableau.isRowStandard_of_no_second_column","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RowStandardTableau.isRowStandard_of_no_second_column","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RowStandardTableau.lean#L74-L84","doc":"**Every filling of a one-column shape is row-standard.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RowStandardTableau.instFintypeRowStandardTab","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RowStandardTableau.instFintypeRowStandardTab","kind":"instance","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RowStandardTableau.lean#L65-L66","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RowStandardTableau.instDecidableIsRowStandard","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RowStandardTableau.instDecidableIsRowStandard","kind":"instance","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RowStandardTableau.lean#L62-L63","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RowStandardTableau.instCoeOutRowStandardTabTableau","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RowStandardTableau.instCoeOutRowStandardTabTableau","kind":"instance","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RowStandardTableau.lean#L60-L60","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RowStandardTab","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RowStandardTab","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RowStandardTableau.lean#L56-L58","doc":"A **row-standard tableau** of shape `μ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RowStandardTableau.IsRowStandard","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RowStandardTableau.IsRowStandard","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RowStandardTableau.lean#L47-L54","doc":"**Row-standard**: within any one row, label order agrees with column order.\n\nStated as the single implication `same row → earlier column → smaller label`. The converse\nfollows from it (both patterns are determined by the filling, which is a bijection), so this is\nthe convenient form to *use*: a hypothesis about columns discharges a goal about labels. ","signatureChunk":0}]}